WEBVTT

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:03.060
We're leaving!

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.200
Good work!

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.690
I thought I was going to die.

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:12.690
If you're going to sleep, go to bed.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:14.320
Sorry.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.030
You were up all night, too, but you seem fine.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.190
From: Yoshiyuki Hatori
Sub: About the manuscript
I received everything.
-- Hatori

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:26.210
That's it?

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:31.230
And I missed the deadline again.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.180
Tori's probably angry.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:41.110
Are you drawing me again?

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:43.230
You've always been obsessed with that.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:45.150
Just let me do it.

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:46.820
Everything's cleaned up.

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:52.840
Why don't you try doing a self portrait instead?

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.010
I can't take it anymore!

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.220
I'm starving!

00:00:57.750 --> 00:00:59.740
Hey, don't move.

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.710
Jeez, watch it.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:06.750
You don't want to fall and break your hand.

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:09.290
Sorry!

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:12.660
Hey, what are you doing?

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:14.980
Are you eating properly?

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.510
It feels like you lost weight.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.380
You think so?

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.530
You need to eat even if Hatori...

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.060
...doesn't come around to feed you!

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:23.590
And really, you should cook yourself.

00:01:23.590 --> 00:01:25.520
Rice is the staple of the Japanese people!

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:28.490
But making rice is such a pain in the ass.

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:30.130
A pain?

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:32.280
How lazy are you?

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:35.680
No wonder you're so skinny.

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.860
Stop tickling me!

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:39.540
Stop!

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:40.910
Don't, I'm really ticklish there!

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.680
Promise you'll let me draw you naked next time,

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:44.660
and I'll stop.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:46.820
Ah, how dirty!

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:52.290
Um...

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:01.040
Just go with the flow and write him an apology email.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:03.410
You always miss the deadline,

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:05.530
so I'm sure he'll be fine soon.

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:07.750
Y-You think that would work?

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:09.610
But...

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.430
I've got this really bad feeling.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:34.550
jounetsu tte kyuu ni wa michisuu sugiru

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:34.550
The concept of passion is full of so many unknowns

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:40.090
hanshateki hikiau youna tsuyoi jiryoku

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:40.090
A strong magnetic force is pulling us closer

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:44.720
risei no boudaarain karuku koete

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:44.720
Barely crossing the borderline of rationality

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:50.520
arawareta sono hi kara sorasenai

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:50.520
Ever since you appeared in my life, I can't turn away

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:55.530
itazura na unmei konsenchuu no kanjou ni

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:55.530
Whether it's my mischievous fate or conflicting emotions

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:58.360
rikutsu toka tsuuyou shin ai nda

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:58.360
Logic doesn't apply to them

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:03.740
te wo nobaseba wakaru

00:02:58.360 --> 00:03:03.740
If I reach out my hand

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:06.120
hajimete no kimochi

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:06.120
Will you understand my feelings?

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:10.500
sekai ichi kimi ni koi wo shiteru

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:10.500
I'm in love with you, the greatest person in the world

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:14.880
ichibyou goto motto suki ni naru

00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:14.880
I love you more and more every second

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:21.010
happi endo ni wa mada tooi

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:21.010
We're still far from a happy ending

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:29.980
kanaetai yo futari dake no sutoorii

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:29.980
But I want to make it come true

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.440
tsuzuite yuku

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.440
Our story continues

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:42.140
Sorry about what happened...

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.410
No, that's not it.

00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:48.230
I am truly sorry about the other day.

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:50.160
That sounds too stiff...

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.180
I wrote him an email to apologize,

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:56.290
but I still haven't heard from Tori in a week.

00:03:57.410 --> 00:04:00.300
I really went over the deadline this last time.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:03.460
I guess he won't forgive me...

00:04:03.460 --> 00:04:05.250
...unless I properly apologize.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.800
The light in his room was definitely on...

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.830
<i>Connecting you to the voice mail service.</i>

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:33.340
You're persistent.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:38.270
Yeah, because you wouldn't open your door sooner.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.550
I'm sorry.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:43.720
I told you I would get it done on time,

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:46.000
but I missed the deadline again.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:48.380
I must've caused you trouble.

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:53.310
I'm not mad because you missed the deadline.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.000
That happens all the time.

00:04:56.410 --> 00:05:00.050
Well, I do always feel bad about it.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.510
Then what are you mad about?

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:07.970
Why are you looking at me like that?

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.870
I was pissed off because
Yanase was hugging you.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:14.120
What?

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:17.780
I don't want you to let other guys touch you.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.780
Especially not him!

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:22.500
Yuu's a friend!

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:27.080
Why do you always act like he's your enemy?

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:29.260
Do you really not know why?

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:33.040
Well, I have an idea...

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:37.790
But that was totally normal
contact between friends!

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:44.150
Wh-What are you doing?

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:45.750
Stop it!

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:49.130
If you listen to me, then I'll stop.

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:53.380
I can't...

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:57.030
Last night, I was up all night...

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:58.170
Yoshino?

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:00.130
I'm sorry.

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:02.990
I'm so sleepy.

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:13.180
I slept really well.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:15.700
Huh?

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:18.580
What am I doing over at Tori's place?

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:21.420
You're up.

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:23.440
I made breakfast, so hurry up and eat.

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:29.950
Your food is always so good!

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:31.840
You think so?

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.710
He seems like he's in a better mood.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:43.340
Oh, that reminds me.

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:45.580
I'm going to be gone on
Wednesday and Thursday.

00:06:45.580 --> 00:06:47.310
I'm going to a hot spring with Yuu.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:50.790
This is the first I've heard of it.

00:06:50.790 --> 00:06:53.220
Well, I never had a good time to tell you.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:56.090
I wanted to invite you, too,

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:59.600
but the weekend is never
good for Yuu and me.

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:03.610
But I definitely wanted to give
you the storyboard before I left,

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:06.610
so I brought it over last night.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:09.450
I pulled an all nighter to finish it.

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:14.620
Do you even remember what's on that day?

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:17.450
Oh, was there something?

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:20.600
I can get you the
supplementary material by tomorrow.

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:22.890
I'll look at the storyboard later.

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:24.590
I'm too busy today.

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:26.630
Eat and then go home.

00:07:28.110 --> 00:07:29.860
H-Hey, what's your problem?

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:31.510
I worked really hard to-

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:32.460
Hey!

00:07:34.830 --> 00:07:36.430
Oh, screw you.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:38.140
You blockhead!

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:49.650
What the hell am I doing?

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:53.160
I came to apologize,
but I started a new fight.

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:58.740
He's not even coming after me either.

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:03.610
I have no idea what's going on in his head.

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:07.500
That's so cute!

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:10.180
I came to the hot-springs...

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:13.250
...without resolving the fight,
or saying another word to Tori.

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:16.140
I wonder what he's doing right now.

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:26.900
I can't eat another bite!

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:29.560
That was even better than I imagined!

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:31.610
And the bath was really spacious and good.

00:08:32.750 --> 00:08:34.660
O-Oh, yeah...

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.900
Oh, just stop it already.

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:42.420
There's no point to waste
time thinking about him.

00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:44.620
Pardon the intrusion.

00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:53.300
Happy Birthday.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.110
Oh, yeah.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:58.680
It's my birthday today.

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:01.370
I had this prepared in secret.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:02.830
You weren't expecting it, were you?

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:06.420
No, thanks!

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:11.940
Do you even remember what's on that day?

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:16.570
Is this why he was upset?

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:20.330
Maybe he had something
prepared for me, too.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:24.830
It is my first birthday since
we've started going out.

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:28.430
Oh, yeah, until now he's...

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:31.880
Oh, I've always wanted to read these!

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.640
Aren't they out of print though?

00:09:33.940 --> 00:09:36.220
I happened to find them
in a used book shop.

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:39.860
Oh my god! These are so out of print!

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:41.850
Where did you find them?!

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:44.360
I got them so you can be inspired
for your future works.

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:46.270
That's my job, as your editor.

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:47.480
It's not a big deal.

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:51.650
None of it was romantic per se,

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:56.770
but I wonder if he had gone
all over to find them.

00:09:57.780 --> 00:10:00.240
Which makes me wonder if...

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:04.320
...I've ever given or done
anything for him in return.

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:07.410
Ever since I've started this job,

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:09.600
I've only thought about what I needed.

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:15.770
I guess you're bored if Hatori's not around.

00:10:15.770 --> 00:10:16.380
Huh?

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:19.090
I bet you were just thinking about how...

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:21.090
...this would be so much
more fun if he was here.

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:22.880
Wh-What are you talking about?!

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:24.230
I wasn't thinking that at all!

00:10:24.230 --> 00:10:26.350
I came here to get away from work,

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:28.690
and I wouldn't be able to
do that with him here.

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:32.200
And then, he's always so fussy and
complaining about every little thing.

00:10:32.200 --> 00:10:35.150
I guess, but that's his job.

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:39.780
Wh-Which is why I don't want
to see his face on my days off!

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:41.870
But the cake!

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:43.030
Let's eat the cake!

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:45.950
I don't really like sweet food,

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:47.560
so go and eat as much as you want.

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:49.630
Let me have the champagne.

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:51.960
You don't like wines, right?

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:53.310
Yeah...

00:10:55.700 --> 00:10:58.150
Wow, this cake is delicious!

00:10:58.420 --> 00:10:59.830
Thanks, Yuu!

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:11.830
Wh-What's wrong?

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:13.880
Is there something on my face?

00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:16.370
I asked you before to let me
draw you in the nude, remember?

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:17.570
So can I now?

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:20.850
Hey, I never agreed to that!

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:23.100
And you're drunk!

00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:25.080
Stop being such a stiff.

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:27.830
Anyway, I'm not drunk at all.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.090
Come on. Get naked.

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:31.580
Stop that!

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:37.410
You know, you could do something
for me every once in a while, too.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:41.760
This is something I want to do,

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.840
so can't you just cooperate and do it?

00:11:46.300 --> 00:11:49.400
Fine, but upper body only.

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:51.010
Sure.

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:52.090
That's fine.

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:54.750
Then can you sit on that chair?

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:16.630
Don't you get bored of drawing me?

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:18.340
Nope.

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:21.880
After all, I love you.

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:22.880
What?

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:25.840
I love your build.

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:29.430
I see. The bones...

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:32.960
And your bones, too.

00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:41.490
Are you trying to say you really love me?

00:12:46.080 --> 00:12:48.240
What the hell is going on?

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:51.910
I'm really thirsty so I'm
going to go get a drink...

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:53.250
Do you want me to get you something, too?

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:57.380
What?

00:12:58.680 --> 00:13:01.200
Remember how you asked me
if I was in love with anyone.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:03.530
Do you still want to know?

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:07.570
If you want to know, I'll tell you.

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:18.540
Remember how you asked me if
I was in love with anyone.

00:13:19.370 --> 00:13:20.530
Do you still want to know?

00:13:21.190 --> 00:13:22.860
If you want to know, I'll tell you.

00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:25.850
I don't...

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:29.310
M-My phone!

00:13:29.310 --> 00:13:30.620
Who could be calling me?

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:34.220
Hello?

00:13:34.220 --> 00:13:34.810
It's me.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:36.380
T-Tori?

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:37.700
Can you talk?

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:41.690
Uh, the reception is pretty bad here.

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:42.630
I'll try moving somewhere else.

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:44.740
I'm going outside.

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:51.960
Hello?

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:53.880
I looked at your storyboard revisions.

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:55.890
They look fine.

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:59.670
There are a few places where I'd
like you to change the dialog,

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:02.340
but all in all, it's fine the way it is.

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:04.050
Okay. Got it.

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.900
I'll start drawing it as soon as I get back.

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:09.710
Tori?

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:11.410
Sorry.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:12.540
Yes?

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:16.220
I'm sorry for acting so childish the other day.

00:14:17.450 --> 00:14:19.700
It's...fine.

00:14:21.660 --> 00:14:23.920
God, what is wrong with me?

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:27.310
How could I let him apologize to me again?

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:30.430
I was the one in the wrong.

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:31.840
Are you still angry at me?

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:36.060
No, I wouldn't say that.

00:14:36.630 --> 00:14:38.820
I didn't mean to crash your
vacation with this call.

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:41.100
That's all I have to say, so...

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:42.830
Hang on.

00:14:42.830 --> 00:14:45.020
Happy Birthday, Yoshino.

00:14:46.350 --> 00:14:47.190
See ya.

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:51.110
He could've easily waited until tomorrow...

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:52.700
...to tell me that thing about work.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:54.770
Did he maybe...

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:57.710
...call me just to say that last bit?

00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:02.920
Damn it!

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:05.590
Why does everything just happen like this?!

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:08.840
Chiaki. What's wrong?

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:11.260
I'm sorry.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:13.660
S-Something happened at home.

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:16.040
I've got to go back.

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:17.230
You mean now?

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:19.480
Can't you go home tomorrow morning?

00:15:19.970 --> 00:15:22.410
No, I've got to go right now.

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:24.800
Before the day is over.

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:27.880
I'm so sorry!

00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:29.240
I'm being very selfish.

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:32.740
I'm really sorry, but can I owe you one?

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:40.300
Yoshino...

00:15:40.780 --> 00:15:42.340
H-Hey...

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:44.190
Weren't you at the hot springs?

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:48.880
I was, but I guess I came home.

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:51.380
Did something happen?

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:54.370
N-No.

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:59.360
I just really wanted to see your face...

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:03.640
I mean,

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:05.740
I really wanted to get some work done!

00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:07.260
I just came to the wrong apartment!

00:16:08.850 --> 00:16:11.540
Can you please say that again?

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:13.780
What, exactly?

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:16.700
That you really wanted to see my face.

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:17.410
Did you mean it?

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:19.410
I don't even remember saying that!

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:24.550
It's late, so why don't you spend the night?

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:27.500
You can start working tomorrow.

00:16:27.950 --> 00:16:28.670
Sure...

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:32.330
Can I get you a beer?

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:34.640
You know...

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:35.530
Yeah?

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:38.180
I...

00:16:39.520 --> 00:16:42.560
I forgot that today was my birthday.

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:49.360
Is that why you came back home?

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:51.190
You're ridiculous.

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:53.530
Hey!

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:56.570
I do feel bad about it.

00:16:57.220 --> 00:16:58.640
You don't have to apologize.

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:02.890
Just having you here is enough for me.

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:04.990
What the hell?

00:17:05.390 --> 00:17:07.710
It's not like I haven't seen
his face for twenty years,

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:10.650
so why am I getting all fluttery now?

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:12.260
Yoshino.

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:14.220
What's that?

00:17:14.840 --> 00:17:16.040
It's a present.

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:18.350
I'm glad I could give it to you today.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:21.630
Tori!

00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:24.490
Thanks!

00:17:25.560 --> 00:17:27.040
Whoa, that's really heavy!

00:17:27.040 --> 00:17:29.050
What the heck is in here?

00:17:31.150 --> 00:17:32.320
What is this?

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:34.680
It's paper for manuscripts. Can't you tell?

00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:38.360
I'm supposed to be happy that I got this?

00:17:38.360 --> 00:17:41.120
I thought it would be better if
I gave you something practical.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:43.110
You could've given me something...

00:17:43.110 --> 00:17:45.240
...a little more romantic for my birthday!

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:46.950
Like what?

00:17:46.950 --> 00:17:48.300
Well...

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:51.350
I mean, I don't have anything
specific in mind...

00:17:58.830 --> 00:17:59.980
Tori?

00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:02.260
Then I'll give you myself.

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:04.320
What?

00:18:04.320 --> 00:18:06.050
Aren't you embarrassed,

00:18:06.050 --> 00:18:07.840
saying cheesy stuff like that?

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:10.150
If you don't want me, that's fine, too.

00:18:10.760 --> 00:18:14.110
I-I didn't say that...

00:18:18.060 --> 00:18:19.030
Yoshino...

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:32.650
You're not resisting tonight?

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:35.040
Is that a complaint?

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:36.040
No.

00:18:39.400 --> 00:18:41.460
You smell different from normal.

00:18:43.020 --> 00:18:44.810
I used some shampoo they had at the inn.

00:18:45.550 --> 00:18:47.310
Did you get in the bath with him?

00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:50.560
Well, they had a big public bathing area...

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:52.190
Hey...

00:18:54.280 --> 00:18:56.070
What the hell are you doing?!

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:57.990
I don't want you...

00:18:57.990 --> 00:18:59.950
...showing your naked
body to any other guy!

00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:01.450
What the hell?

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:03.450
Then I can't go to a bath
or hot spring ever again!

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:04.380
If it was up to me,

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:07.040
I'd forbid you to show your
naked body to another man again,

00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:09.410
but I guess a public bath is all right.

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:12.330
But I don't want you showing
yourself to Yanase, ever again.

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:16.460
Promise me you'll never go anywhere
alone with him ever again.

00:19:16.830 --> 00:19:18.830
Why do I have to promise
something like that?

00:19:20.430 --> 00:19:21.920
Isn't it obvious?

00:19:22.360 --> 00:19:23.220
Because I get jealous!

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:24.720
Huh?

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:28.960
You write about romance,
can't you just figure it out?!

00:19:28.960 --> 00:19:30.770
Figure it out?

00:19:31.400 --> 00:19:32.840
Jealous?

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:37.610
Does he have any idea what he
sounds like when he says stuff like this?

00:19:37.930 --> 00:19:40.300
If you understand,
then I want you to swear.

00:19:43.680 --> 00:19:45.830
F-Fine!

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:48.130
I promise.

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:50.700
You mean it?

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:53.500
Of course I do.

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:55.840
Chiaki...

00:20:00.660 --> 00:20:02.010
So what do you think?

00:20:03.910 --> 00:20:05.400
No, come on!

00:20:05.770 --> 00:20:08.940
Even shojo manga has its limits!

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:11.020
Yeah, that was kind of creepy.

00:20:11.380 --> 00:20:14.100
I-It was just a suggestion!

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:17.850
But it's a suggestion you came up with.

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:19.370
That's so funny!

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:24.230
You can all stop laughing now!

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:27.240
Tori!

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:29.410
What's going on in here?

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:32.550
Hatori, you've got to hear this!

00:20:32.550 --> 00:20:34.240
No, you don't!

00:20:34.720 --> 00:20:35.770
Hear what?

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:39.620
So Yoshino here was suggesting that
on the main character's birthday,

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:44.270
their love interest asks if they
can give the gift of them self!

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:45.440
I mean, come on?

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:46.920
Who would ever say something like that?

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:51.410
He's pissed.

00:20:51.410 --> 00:20:53.190
He is so pissed.

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:56.740
I keep telling them, it's just a suggestion.

00:20:57.000 --> 00:21:01.020
I was thinking myself that
it was kind of weird.

00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:01.940
Weird?

00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:03.870
Not weird, per se.

00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:05.030
Nobody would ever say that.

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:09.450
I'd like to see what kind of guy
would ever drop a line like that.

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:13.200
This is bad.

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:14.520
This is really bad!

00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:16.850
I mean, when he said it to me,
it kind of made my heart race,

00:21:16.850 --> 00:21:19.670
so I thought I could maybe use it...

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:23.220
Then again, it's not like I was going
to use it like he said it, word for word!

00:21:23.890 --> 00:21:25.460
Anyway, I'd argue...

00:21:25.460 --> 00:21:27.340
...that these kinds of lines
are an occupational hazard.

00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:28.910
You're right.

00:21:28.910 --> 00:21:31.140
It might be a bit clichéd.

00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:34.230
I hope you can come up
with something better.

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:38.540
I'll try my best! I'll really try my best!

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:42.360
His eyes are not smiling.

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:44.860
Yup, they are definitely not smiling!

00:21:46.210 --> 00:21:48.600
I've got a bad feeling about this!

